Backlog tail, Selected item/items:

1. Frontend cleanup — six targeted reductions across the web-ui frontend
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/keyboard-bar.js': Replace scrollKeyMap with a module-scope SCROLL_KEYS Set
        - Replace the object with Set(['ArrowUp','ArrowDown','PageUp','PageDown']); change scrollKeyMap[event.key] !== undefined to SCROLL_KEYS.has(event.key)
        - The -40/40 arrow values are re-hardcoded downstream and 'pageUp'/'pageDown' are never referenced, so nothing is lost
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/api-client.js': Collapse renderPrompt onto #post
        - Body becomes this.#post('/api/render-prompt', { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ domain, prompt }) })
        - renderPrompt duplicates #post's fetch + response.ok + error-message logic; leave boot (GET) alone
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/message.js': Inline updateContent
        - At the single call site in clanker-app, replace assistantMsg.updateContent(...) with assistantMsg.content = prevContent + fullText
        - Remove the one-line updateContent method
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/clanker-app.js': Drop the always-true guard ⚠️ revision
        - Remove only the if (!prevContent) conditional; keep assistantMsg.sentChars = totalChars;
        - Add a one-line comment that it seeds the chars-per-prefill-token ratio (consumed by message.js onPrefill for the live token estimates)
        - Dropping the assignment would silently degrade running stats from token-based to char-based
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/messages-box.js': Dedupe setScrollLocked(false)
        - Bind one handler to both focusin and wheel instead of two identical one-liners (#handleFocusIn/#handleWheel)
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/base-component.js' (+ 'content/web-ui/frontend/message.js'): Drop cosmetic comments
        - Remove //All components inherit BaseComponent...
        - Remove the // --- Prefill/Reasoning/Content segment --- markers in message.js #buildStatsLine
        - Keep the // null | 'prefill' | ... phase spec and // Surface a single prompt_progress tick.
2. Backend tidiness — seven refactorings across backend
    [ ] 'content/backend/adapters/disk_adapter.py': Extract _base_dir
        - Add a _base_dir(basepath_token) helper; call it from get_file_paths and get_dir_manifest
        - The ~5× FileAccessError wrapper is out of scope unless a decorator is accepted
        - Leave _resolve_tokenized_path alone: same PUD/SHARED resolution but a different shape
    [ ] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Consolidate the three _get_* fetchers ⚠️ revision
        - Collapse _get_asset_pack / _get_config / _get_file_req into one _fetch(fetch_fn, factory, ...)
        - Preserve both special branches: _get_config's ConfigParseError → Malformed and _get_file_req's IsADirectoryError → Filereq(..., "") (a directory path maps to empty content)
        - A plain _fetch(fetch_fn, factory) handling only NoSuchFile → Missing would drop the directory case and let an accidental directory path raise uncaught
    [ ] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Merge the update/delete pre-flight checks
        - Fold the two identical existence loops (both append to missing_paths) into one loop over parsed.updates + parsed.deletes
    [ ] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/content_shaper.py': Use an explicit placeholder map ⚠️ revision
        - Build an explicit {sentinel: replacement} map instead of introspecting e.Delims.__dict__
        - Include all delims (not just PROMPT_*); a partial map would silently change what .output-template files substitute
        - The isinstance(pair, tuple) and len(pair)==2 filter is dead (every member is a 2-tuple) and can go
        - "order-fragile" isn't a real risk — sentinels are unique, replacements don't nest; the issue is just indirectness
    [ ] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/extractors/map_extractor2.py': Dedupe Numap type guards
        - Route register / set_entity / register_cleanup through a single _assert_entity(entity)
        - Leave prune alone — it takes a list and recurses, so it only partially fits
    [ ] 'content/backend/controller.py': Simplify the POST decorator (medium)
        - Evaluate whether POST can store fn directly with the server passing path, or keep the pass-through wrapper
        - POST handlers take (controller, body, path) vs GET's (controller, params), so a true merge may require GET handlers to also accept path
    [ ] 'content/backend/core/core/entities.py': classproperty → staticmethod (low)
        - Consider making key_name/plural_key staticmethods
        - Requires updating every value-position call site to key_name() (e.g., cfg.data.get(entity_cls.key_name)); plural_key's body changes too
        - Worth it only if already in these files


Backlog tail end


